1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
A self-driving car cannot see the world.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,200
It only ever sees its own view.

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,400
The camera sees a person.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,600
3 metres to my right. 4 metres in front of me.

5
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,000
Right and ahead of WHAT? Of the car.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,400
Turn the car and both words change.

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,000
A map has no ahead. It has north.

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,200
How far the car is turned: cos θ = 0.8, sin θ = 0.6.

9
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,400
What the camera said, into the formula.

10
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,800
2.4 − 2.4 = 0.   1.8 + 3.2 = 5.

11
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:27,200
On the map: 5 metres due north. Same person, new words.

12
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:30,000
Skip that step and the car brakes for somebody who isn't there.

13
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,800
Robot vacuums, AR filters, drones landing. Thousands of times a second.

14
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,000
We learned this at school.

15
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,200
Nobody ever said what for.

16
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,800
Send this to your school friend — and tell them THIS is how it's solved.

17
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:40,000
Follow for the math behind AI. @observer.collapse
